1
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:09,990
Damn it... I wanted to stop 
the raid on the mansion,

2
00:00:09,990 --> 00:00:12,400
but I think I just made it inevitable.

3
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:15,970
Hah! Well, hearin' all that 
sure made me feel good.

4
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:19,000
If that hadn't been a negotiation 
to resolve things peacefully,

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,080
I might have agreed with you.

6
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:25,090
I have to get to the mansion 
as fast as possible!

7
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:26,750
Yet here I am...

8
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,010
To say we're short-handed right 
now is an understatement.

9
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:32,160
Well, I'll go with ya, then.

10
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:32,910
Huh?

11
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:34,840
What?

12
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:36,860
Are you sure you understand?

13
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:40,870
Going to the mansion means 
leaving the Sanctuary.

14
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:42,950
Wouldn't the barrier stop you?

15
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:44,250
Barrier?

16
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:45,440
That ain't a problem.

17
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:46,680
Huh?!

18
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:51,900
Like my sister, I have a 
mixed-blood dad and a human mom.

19
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:54,860
My mixed blood's too thin for it to stop me.

20
00:00:55,210 --> 00:00:59,370
But I heard you and Frederica 
had different fathers!

21
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:02,080
Huh? Well, y'know...

22
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:07,340
My mom had shit for luck and 
shit for taste in men.

23
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,590
You figure it out!

24
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,630
You should've told me that sooner!

25
00:01:17,590 --> 00:01:21,330
I'm already the strongest 
there is, but with these,

26
00:01:21,330 --> 00:01:23,390
I'll be even stronger!

27
00:01:23,650 --> 00:01:27,440
Give us a good show of 
just how strong you are!

28
00:01:28,210 --> 00:01:29,700
You can count on it.

29
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:33,170
No one can run from Reinhard, as they say.

30
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:36,600
He's still alive, and he 
already has his own idiom?

31
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:37,670
Seriously?

32
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,070
Everything's ready here, too.

33
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:44,060
Now we just have to hope Elsa 
and her partner aren't early.

34
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:47,260
I'm counting on you guys and on our enemy!

35
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:49,520
That's the art of war, Natsuki Subaru style!

36
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:51,590
My <i>Reverse Fuurinkazan</i>!

37
00:01:52,470 --> 00:01:54,130
Th-That's so cool!

38
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:57,230
Thanks for all the help, you two morons!

39
00:01:57,230 --> 00:02:00,610
Can't you just thank people 
normally, you one moron?!

40
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:01,640
So anyway, Ram...

41
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,760
The rest is up to you.

42
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,830
Fine. Do as you like.

43
00:02:05,830 --> 00:02:08,600
I'm going to do as I like from this point on.

44
00:02:16,770 --> 00:02:17,400
Ram...

45
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:21,200
Don't do anything crazy.

46
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:23,790
Is that for you to say, Barusu?

47
00:02:23,790 --> 00:02:24,660
Don't make me laugh.

48
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:28,410
Okay, people!

49
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:31,180
Sorry this has all been so irregular, but...

50
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:32,880
Subaru-sama,

51
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:35,050
you need not worry about us.

52
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:39,700
Our internal officer has 
already told us everything.

53
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:43,940
Go on, get moving!

54
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:46,710
But you should probably wipe 
your nose off when it bleeds.

55
00:02:46,710 --> 00:02:48,620
You don't want Petra to be disappointed!

56
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:50,880
Thanks, you guys!

57
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:51,480
But...

58
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:55,230
Subaru-sama, just give 
up and let us help you!

59
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,440
Um, who's your internal offic—

60
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:59,030
Off we go!

61
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:33,880
So the three idiots hitched the carriage 
to their very clever ground dragon

62
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:35,620
and set off for the mansion.

63
00:04:36,450 --> 00:04:38,330
All right, I understand.

64
00:04:38,330 --> 00:04:41,120
Honestly, what am I going to do with him?

65
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:42,260
Is that all?

66
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:44,920
I guess I am still a little angry.

67
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:48,960
Did Subaru really mean it 
when he said he loved me?

68
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:52,980
Barusu cares about you more than anyone else.

69
00:04:53,330 --> 00:04:55,290
Right. Thank you.

70
00:04:55,290 --> 00:04:59,070
Emilia-sama, does your return mean that...

71
00:04:59,070 --> 00:05:00,190
The trial?

72
00:05:00,810 --> 00:05:04,840
Yes. I was able to confront my past,

73
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:06,570
but it seems there are two more trials to go.

74
00:05:07,090 --> 00:05:10,920
So I'll have to go into 
the graveyard again later.

75
00:05:15,070 --> 00:05:17,990
You truly have grown stronger.

76
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:22,960
Emilia-sama, I am truly sorry.

77
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,120
What brought this on?

78
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:29,450
This is the first time I've ever 
lowered my head and meant it.

79
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:35,620
Before now, I didn't believe that 
you would get back on your feet.

80
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:40,010
But here you are now, 
standing in front of me,

81
00:05:40,010 --> 00:05:41,950
with your chest high and 
your eyes facing forward.

82
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:45,900
You only lose a few points for the 
tear marks remaining on your cheeks.

83
00:05:46,230 --> 00:05:48,860
Huh? Oh, darn it!

84
00:05:49,730 --> 00:05:55,460
So did you help Subaru and Otto-kun 
because you thought I was just a crybaby?

85
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:58,120
Don't be silly. It was you I helped,

86
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:01,210
and you who determined that 
helping would be worth my while.

87
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:05,360
It... was? But why?

88
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:08,590
What made you decide to help me?

89
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:13,960
When asking for something, 
one must show one's sincerity.

90
00:06:19,290 --> 00:06:21,230
I beg of you, Emilia-sama.

91
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:25,030
Please save my master, Roswaal-sama.

92
00:06:25,470 --> 00:06:26,740
Roswaal?

93
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:30,490
He has become possessed by delusions.

94
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:35,700
Delusions that have bound his soul 
like a curse for a long, long time.

95
00:06:36,690 --> 00:06:39,270
I might not have have minded that.

96
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:41,980
Even if he wouldn't look at me,

97
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:44,480
even if he only thought of me as a tool...

98
00:06:45,710 --> 00:06:46,430
Ram...

99
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:51,260
But his delusions have already strayed 
from the path toward a clean conclusion.

100
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:53,970
His wish has lost its direction,

101
00:06:53,970 --> 00:06:56,890
and he clings to words written 
purely for aesthetics.

102
00:06:57,720 --> 00:07:00,350
Please break through that.

103
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:04,310
What should I do?

104
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:07,030
Assume the royal throne.

105
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:12,830
Once you assume the throne of Lugunica,

106
00:07:12,830 --> 00:07:15,100
Roswaal-sama's wish will be fulfilled.

107
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:17,810
Even if he's walked astray 
from his path for so long,

108
00:07:17,810 --> 00:07:20,210
the day his wish comes to fruition will come.

109
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:24,350
Please tell Roswaal-sama that.

110
00:07:24,850 --> 00:07:28,660
Give him a reason to live through 
both present and the future.

111
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:32,630
Please, Emilia-sama.

112
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:37,600
Please save him.

113
00:07:49,490 --> 00:07:55,490
I don't quite understand what my becoming 
the ruler has to do with saving Roswaal.

114
00:07:56,240 --> 00:08:01,340
I don't think I can truly understand 
your wishes just yet, either.

115
00:08:02,210 --> 00:08:02,830
But...

116
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:07,790
This is the first time you've 
ever asked anything of me.

117
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,590
All right, Ram.

118
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:14,870
You believed in me, and I want to repay that.

119
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:19,350
I'm sure that's something I 
have to start on by myself now.

120
00:08:32,530 --> 00:08:34,610
Would you mind...

121
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:38,700
if I offered my congratulations to you, too?

122
00:08:45,670 --> 00:08:46,810
That's close enough.

123
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:50,050
Well, well...

124
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:53,620
What a fine welcome this is, Emilia-sama.

125
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:57,890
Despite how I may appear, 
my concern for you is genuine.

126
00:08:57,890 --> 00:09:00,820
You could even say I pity you.

127
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:02,800
Pity... me?

128
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:06,600
Yes, I pity you from the bottom of my heart.

129
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:10,990
You have no idea how to be loved other 
than to do what people expect of you,

130
00:09:10,990 --> 00:09:14,860
yet you are forced to confront 
a past that you never wanted.

131
00:09:16,210 --> 00:09:18,820
Allow me to congratulate you,

132
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:23,170
with all of the pity and 
compassion I can offer.

133
00:09:23,170 --> 00:09:25,810
Well done overcoming the trial!

134
00:09:25,810 --> 00:09:28,830
I was convinced that you 
were incapable of it.

135
00:09:29,570 --> 00:09:32,560
It's hard to thank you when 
you congratulate me that way.

136
00:09:33,090 --> 00:09:36,180
You said you didn't think I could do it.

137
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,800
Are you reconsidering that?

138
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:42,310
You're right. I know I've 
worried you a great deal.

139
00:09:43,290 --> 00:09:45,660
All I've been able to do is lose my nerve.

140
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:50,270
I've caused so much trouble for 
Puck, for Subaru... for everyone.

141
00:09:50,850 --> 00:09:53,580
But they all saved me.

142
00:09:53,970 --> 00:09:55,770
I was utterly useless,

143
00:09:55,770 --> 00:09:57,340
and they lent me a helping hand.

144
00:09:57,770 --> 00:10:01,550
It made me realize that I can't 
just go on being discouraged.

145
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:07,400
You say the same things Subaru-kun did.

146
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:09,950
Are you simply repeating his words?

147
00:10:09,950 --> 00:10:10,790
Roswaal-sama!

148
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:14,360
Your borrowed words, the place 
that has been prepared for you,

149
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:19,010
and even your attempts at the trial were 
decisions made only after the stage was set.

150
00:10:19,010 --> 00:10:22,980
Yet even knowing that, Subaru-kun 
urges you to do terrible things.

151
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:25,140
That's not true! Subaru wants—

152
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:26,490
We both know him.

153
00:10:26,490 --> 00:10:28,590
He was not speaking with logic or reason,

154
00:10:28,590 --> 00:10:31,730
but only gave you an exceptionally 
loud pep talk. Am I wrong?

155
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:34,010
He imposed his self-satisfaction on you,

156
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:38,130
forcing you to fit his ideal with the 
emotional assertion that you could do it.

157
00:10:38,130 --> 00:10:40,840
I understand. I truly do.

158
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,700
After all, he and I...

159
00:10:43,050 --> 00:10:45,660
are two of a kind.

160
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:49,350
You and Subaru are two of a kind?

161
00:10:49,350 --> 00:10:50,750
What does that mean?

162
00:10:50,750 --> 00:10:54,800
That we both force our ideals 
upon the women we love.

163
00:10:56,350 --> 00:10:58,370
I'm sure he has spoiled you

164
00:10:58,370 --> 00:11:01,220
and treated you with 
utmost kindness and care.

165
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:05,740
He never even considered that you 
are not a normal girl, did he?

166
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:10,390
The you he loves is the ideal you 
that lives within his own mind.

167
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,350
Am I wrong?

168
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,030
Is that all?

169
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:26,600
That's the only thing that makes 
you think you're like him?

170
00:11:27,530 --> 00:11:29,600
If that's all you want to say...

171
00:11:30,150 --> 00:11:33,470
You and Subaru aren't the same at all.

172
00:11:34,740 --> 00:11:39,130
Subaru told me that I was a pain in the ass.

173
00:11:39,540 --> 00:11:40,340
What?

174
00:11:40,630 --> 00:11:45,050
He asked who I thought I was, 
causing trouble for him when he's done so much.

175
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:49,860
He told me not to keep brooding 
over what's in the past.

176
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:54,150
He said I was all talk, 
and he couldn't put up with it.

177
00:11:55,010 --> 00:11:57,570
And everything he said was right.

178
00:11:57,980 --> 00:12:02,610
I was weak, all talk, 
and insufficient in every way.

179
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:06,110
Subaru truly sees me for who I am.

180
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:10,180
So I know you and Subaru are nothing alike.

181
00:12:13,140 --> 00:12:14,790
When I want to do something,

182
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:17,260
when I wish I could change,

183
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:20,240
he takes my hand and helps me.

184
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:23,010
He taught me that there are people 
who would say that for me.

185
00:12:23,010 --> 00:12:25,570
You do not think he was simply deceiving you?

186
00:12:25,570 --> 00:12:28,210
All to tactfully get you back on your feet?

187
00:12:28,210 --> 00:12:30,480
No. He wasn't lying.

188
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:34,580
What Subaru felt when he said he 
believed in me won't turn into a lie.

189
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:36,190
I won't let it.

190
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:38,060
I'll turn the lies into wishes.

191
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:42,770
That's what I need to do right now,
 and what I want to do.

192
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:52,720
You just continue to change.

193
00:12:54,530 --> 00:12:58,670
This is exceedingly difficult 
for me to accept.

194
00:13:02,290 --> 00:13:03,470
Roswaal?

195
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:06,210
Your decision is priceless,

196
00:13:06,210 --> 00:13:08,430
and your will to walk forward is noble.

197
00:13:08,930 --> 00:13:12,100
This is precisely why I pity you.

198
00:13:12,850 --> 00:13:16,100
The decision you've made that 
justifies you getting hurt

199
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:19,270
is already meaningless in this 
world that will soon end.

200
00:13:19,270 --> 00:13:21,280
The world... will end?

201
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:24,570
More precisely, it is moving toward its end.

202
00:13:24,930 --> 00:13:27,170
This world has strayed from the correct path

203
00:13:27,170 --> 00:13:30,290
and now proceeds toward 
the wrong destination.

204
00:13:30,290 --> 00:13:33,620
The Sanctuary and the royal selection 
have already lost all meaning.

205
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:35,100
Roswaal?

206
00:13:35,610 --> 00:13:37,710
Why do you sound like you're giving up?

207
00:13:38,090 --> 00:13:41,570
Weren't you... Weren't you and 
I the ones who started this?

208
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:44,630
And you'd give up before it's over?
 I won't allow that!

209
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:48,340
Then what is it you wish to do?

210
00:13:48,570 --> 00:13:50,330
I don't know!

211
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:52,520
But what's wrong is wrong!

212
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:53,800
Don't give up!

213
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,600
That's just too selfish!

214
00:13:56,480 --> 00:14:00,140
You really do sound just like Subaru-kun.

215
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:07,180
How much of your boastful speech 
can ever be realized, I wonder?

216
00:14:07,550 --> 00:14:11,060
That's what I'm about to show you.

217
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:15,000
In the graveyard... no, 
outside the Sanctuary, too.

218
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:18,180
Emilia-sama...

219
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:20,000
I'm going now, Ram.

220
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,960
I promise I'll take care of 
the favor you asked of me.

221
00:14:33,350 --> 00:14:36,320
It was my teacher and I who started it.

222
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:39,820
That is the one thing you 
got wrong, Emilia-sama.

223
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:56,510
It seems her resolve is far 
stronger than I realized.

224
00:14:56,990 --> 00:15:00,960
Roswaal-sama, how much of our 
conversation did you hear?

225
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:04,300
I saw you kneel before her.

226
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:06,170
You are quite the actress.

227
00:15:06,770 --> 00:15:11,470
I have heard that you 
assisted them with Garfiel.

228
00:15:11,470 --> 00:15:14,890
Of course, I know you believed 
it was the right thing to do.

229
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:19,560
What do you intend to do now?

230
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:23,430
What I desire has not changed,

231
00:15:23,810 --> 00:15:26,740
though I am now forced to 
work a bit harder for it.

232
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:27,490
What shall I...

233
00:15:27,490 --> 00:15:30,530
Remain here and await Emilia-sama's return.

234
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:34,040
If no one were here to 
welcome her brave soul back,

235
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:38,370
even my own heart would ache for her.

236
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:54,320
<i>The reason I took that bet was because it 
seemed like my best chance at getting my wish.</i>

237
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:57,040
Hello, Ram-san.

238
00:15:57,670 --> 00:16:00,770
It's a lovely evening, isn't it?
 The breeze feels so cool.

239
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:03,730
You're the boy who was with Barusu.

240
00:16:03,730 --> 00:16:07,840
Natsuki-san just can't seem 
to see you as an enemy.

241
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:08,820
If he's right,

242
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:14,200
I believe we can assist you in 
getting what you <i>really</i> want.

243
00:16:15,730 --> 00:16:16,700
So annoying.

244
00:16:17,010 --> 00:16:17,760
Huh?

245
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:20,160
I said you're annoying.

246
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,700
Give me more details.

247
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:26,380
That's my idea.

248
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:27,740
What do you think?

249
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:33,970
If you want my help, I have three conditions.

250
00:16:34,510 --> 00:16:38,560
First, I'm strongly in favor 
of taking Garfiel down a notch.

251
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:42,630
But after you do that, 
you must leave him to me.

252
00:16:43,070 --> 00:16:43,980
Got it.

253
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:46,320
Then there's Emilia-sama.

254
00:16:46,870 --> 00:16:48,900
Make Barusu do something about her.

255
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:52,360
I think that will be up to 
Natsuki-san and Emilia-sama.

256
00:16:52,870 --> 00:16:56,110
So... I feel as if the third 
one is going to be a doozy.

257
00:16:56,470 --> 00:16:57,570
Fool.

258
00:16:57,570 --> 00:17:01,870
Just don't tell Barusu why I took this bet.

259
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:04,890
I don't want to give up my last endgame.

260
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:24,030
I suppose it would be easy to get 
here if one used clairvoyance.

261
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:29,010
Did I not order you to wait for Emilia-sama?

262
00:17:29,010 --> 00:17:31,130
Yes, you did.

263
00:17:31,130 --> 00:17:32,570
Then tell me.

264
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:36,780
For what reason did you come here?

265
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:38,530
It's simple.

266
00:17:39,140 --> 00:17:40,710
I've come to take you away...

267
00:17:42,030 --> 00:17:44,870
from the witch's delusions.

268
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:49,030
Delusions, eh?

269
00:17:49,030 --> 00:17:52,200
It has been some years since 
you pointed your wand at me,

270
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:56,270
but it's a shame you did so here, 
and that you called them "delusions."

271
00:17:56,270 --> 00:17:59,580
I've always considered them such. 
I just never said it out loud.

272
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:00,930
Is it not obvious?

273
00:18:01,140 --> 00:18:02,410
Obvious...

274
00:18:02,930 --> 00:18:08,440
Well, from your perspective, your humiliating
 days spent yielding to me have been long.

275
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:13,110
I considered your behavior to be your 
way of expressing your devotion.

276
00:18:14,830 --> 00:18:18,250
Beating up Garf served two 
purposes: to fulfill my goal,

277
00:18:18,250 --> 00:18:21,200
and to attempt to rectify his idiocy.

278
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:25,410
I have no idea what they planned 
to do if I hadn't been there.

279
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:30,300
I cannot deny that it all 
worked out well in the end.

280
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:35,140
Subaru-kun will naturally choose to walk 
a fine line in the final confrontation.

281
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:38,560
But the one thing Barusu has 
going for him is his timing.

282
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:42,970
Betting on that one good quality 
he has wasn't a mistake.

283
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:47,730
You have the book, yes?

284
00:18:50,490 --> 00:18:52,980
In the place designated 
for the final showdown,

285
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:55,910
at the stage when you take action yourself,

286
00:18:56,290 --> 00:19:01,410
there's no way you don't have the Tome of 
Wisdom that you rely on above all else.

287
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:05,730
I have never once forgotten

288
00:19:05,730 --> 00:19:10,120
the one and only vow that 
you and I exchanged.

289
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:12,720
Those who wield the sword 
should die by the sword,

290
00:19:12,720 --> 00:19:14,720
those who rely on magic should die by magic,

291
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:17,090
and those who give themselves 
to fire should die by fire.

292
00:19:17,650 --> 00:19:20,840
And those who ask favors of a 
demon should die by that demon.

293
00:19:21,350 --> 00:19:25,680
Whatever one relies upon should be the 
thing that brings about their death.

294
00:19:26,710 --> 00:19:28,960
And now the time has come.

295
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:33,650
Now that I have lost that which 
I desired, I offer myself to you.

296
00:19:34,130 --> 00:19:36,450
If you don't mind that 
I am but an empty husk,

297
00:19:36,450 --> 00:19:40,000
you may do as you please 
with me. That was our vow.

298
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,070
Whether I let you live 
or kill you is up to me.

299
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:45,600
You can finally achieve your retribution.

300
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:49,700
After all...

301
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:53,230
You had no choice but to swear 
loyalty against your will

302
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:57,220
to one of the men who destroyed 
your homeland, and live with him.

303
00:19:57,220 --> 00:20:02,910
Although you had to do it after losing your 
horn and your ability to maintain your form,

304
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:05,260
suffering of this degree is uncommonly rare.

305
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:09,010
There is no pawn more useful than you.

306
00:20:09,010 --> 00:20:11,370
Which is why it is such a shame...

307
00:20:11,370 --> 00:20:13,390
Your decision was just the slightest bit...

308
00:20:13,730 --> 00:20:15,520
premature.

309
00:20:15,520 --> 00:20:20,720
It is impressive that you created a situation in
 which I had to carry the Tome of Wisdom.

310
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:25,650
You should have overlooked this last step 
toward the action I was planning to take.

311
00:20:25,650 --> 00:20:27,530
That alone is the true shame!

312
00:20:31,950 --> 00:20:33,990
This is the precious young 
girl who offered her own life

313
00:20:33,990 --> 00:20:37,340
to save her friend by becoming 
the Sanctuary's core.

314
00:20:37,990 --> 00:20:40,840
But my objective does not involve her.

315
00:20:41,830 --> 00:20:45,760
You intend to use this magic 
crystal to cast great magic?

316
00:20:46,050 --> 00:20:48,780
Great enough to change the weather.

317
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:52,720
In accordance with the Tome, I will 
make snow fall in the Sanctuary.

318
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:55,060
In order to use that magic,

319
00:20:55,940 --> 00:21:00,370
I require tremendous focus and 
a highly delicate use of mana.

320
00:21:00,370 --> 00:21:03,770
If I had been engaged in that,
 you most definitely

321
00:21:03,770 --> 00:21:05,450
could have shot me.

322
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:09,160
There would have been no meaning in that.

323
00:21:09,450 --> 00:21:13,650
And there is meaning in forcing me into 
capitulation when I am in my best condition?

324
00:21:13,650 --> 00:21:17,170
Or did you simply want to destroy 
me as quickly as possible?

325
00:21:17,510 --> 00:21:21,500
No. You truly don't 
understand anything at all.

326
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:27,920
I won't allow your wish to come true.

327
00:21:28,330 --> 00:21:32,970
Being offered a husk of you after your 
wish was realized would mean nothing.

328
00:21:33,540 --> 00:21:36,940
Receiving you in a broken 
state would not satisfy me.

329
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:39,980
Well, how very greedy of you.

330
00:21:40,370 --> 00:21:43,070
But do you believe you can defeat me now?

331
00:21:43,490 --> 00:21:45,480
No, I'm sure I can't.

332
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:49,810
My understanding of your power 
is second only to your teacher's.

333
00:21:49,810 --> 00:21:54,910
Then how, exactly, do you 
intend to achieve your goal?

334
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,620
I cannot win alone.

335
00:21:58,990 --> 00:22:01,600
That much is clear. So...

336
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:07,970
If it's two against one, 
I guess we have the advantage?

337
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:13,810
So this is the main reason you 
agreed to Subaru-kun's plan?!

338
00:22:13,810 --> 00:22:16,060
I told you, Roswaal-sama.

339
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:20,480
I'm going to take you away 
from the witch's delusions.

340
00:22:23,070 --> 00:22:26,850
And I'm just a passing stray spirit.

341
00:22:27,630 --> 00:22:31,470
Well, time to pick up 
where we left off before!

342
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:35,790
Come!

343
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:38,920
As you wish!

344
00:22:49,140 --> 00:22:51,340
I have to run... I have to run!

345
00:22:55,110 --> 00:22:56,560
Rem-san?

346
00:22:57,460 --> 00:23:00,270
But... But, but... That can't...

347
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:03,270
But... Rem-san is...

348
00:23:07,140 --> 00:23:10,140
But... I know this is what Subaru would do!

349
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:11,980
So...

350
00:23:18,180 --> 00:23:19,210
Rem-san...

351
00:23:24,420 --> 00:23:26,670
My, what an adorable little girl.

352
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:35,890
You must be the smaller maid, then?

353
00:23:37,210 --> 00:23:38,670
Are you shaking?

354
00:23:39,570 --> 00:23:40,720
Don't worry.

355
00:23:41,290 --> 00:23:45,090
I'm sure your bowels are 
absolutely beautiful.

356
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:48,170
Good girl.

357
00:23:49,180 --> 00:23:51,030
I'll send you to meet the angels.

358
00:23:51,900 --> 00:23:52,660
Petra!

359
00:23:53,860 --> 00:23:55,410
Frederica-neesama!

360
00:23:55,410 --> 00:23:57,200
You are a bad girl, Petra!

361
00:23:57,580 --> 00:23:59,250
I told you to run away.

362
00:23:59,250 --> 00:24:00,710
You will be punished later!

363
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,670
Right... Right!

364
00:24:04,030 --> 00:24:05,420
How lovely.

365
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:08,510
You must be the bigger maid, then.

366
00:24:08,980 --> 00:24:13,310
I'm so glad you're both together, 
and such good friends at that.

367
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:15,820
I'll lay out your bowels side by side

368
00:24:15,820 --> 00:24:18,310
and find out if their insides 
go well together, too.

369
00:24:18,530 --> 00:24:22,830
From start to finish, not a word 
you've just said makes any sense.

370
00:24:22,830 --> 00:24:24,760
I cannot call it a tasteful way of thinking.

371
00:24:24,760 --> 00:24:26,360
Demihuman blood, I see.

372
00:24:26,360 --> 00:24:31,680
But after an experience in the royal capital 
that nearly killed me, my skills have improved.

373
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:33,110
You can't handle me.

374
00:24:33,540 --> 00:24:37,530
I do wish I could lay blame on the 
person who failed to finish you then.

375
00:24:40,970 --> 00:24:43,620
Petra, get outside the mansion now.

376
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:46,960
B-But... Nee-sama...

377
00:24:49,620 --> 00:24:51,950
I do not know who sent you,

378
00:24:51,950 --> 00:24:54,340
but Petra and I appear to be your targets.

379
00:24:54,690 --> 00:24:55,300
Yes.

380
00:24:56,300 --> 00:24:58,800
Two maids and a little spirit girl.

381
00:24:59,230 --> 00:25:02,430
I've never cut open a spirit, 
so I'm quite excited.

382
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:00,390
Go!

383
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:01,470
Right!

384
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:07,740
Your personality is worse than your taste.

385
00:25:08,120 --> 00:25:09,180
She's a good girl.

386
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:10,690
I am most proud of her!

387
00:25:19,700 --> 00:25:20,730
Nee-sama...

388
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:24,720
Maybe Beatrice-sama can do something!

389
00:25:25,430 --> 00:25:26,200
In here!

390
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:27,790
No...

391
00:25:27,790 --> 00:25:29,290
Here?! No...

392
00:25:29,650 --> 00:25:30,460
Not here, either!

393
00:25:30,770 --> 00:25:31,500
Not here...

394
00:25:33,780 --> 00:25:35,420
She's not here, either.

395
00:25:37,820 --> 00:25:38,890
Nee-sama is...

396
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:41,750
Rem-san is...

397
00:25:55,870 --> 00:25:57,260
Subaru...

398
00:25:58,200 --> 00:25:59,970
Help me!

399
00:26:04,460 --> 00:26:07,370
All right. You got it, Petra.

400
00:26:08,910 --> 00:26:09,830
Huh?

401
00:26:10,580 --> 00:26:14,530
Sorry I'm late, but I'm here to help.

402
00:26:15,260 --> 00:26:17,630
I'm glad you're okay, Petra.

403
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:23,470
It's you, Subaru? You came for us?

404
00:26:23,910 --> 00:26:25,500
It's me, and I did.

405
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:27,600
Subaru, Frederica-neesama is—

406
00:26:27,600 --> 00:26:29,120
Just leave it all to me!

407
00:26:29,120 --> 00:26:33,940
...is what I'd like to say, but if I rush 
in there, I'll be dead in a heartbeat.

408
00:26:34,180 --> 00:26:38,760
So I sent some super-strong 
reinforcements instead.

409
00:26:38,760 --> 00:26:40,680
For a night of reunion,

410
00:26:40,680 --> 00:26:43,530
the people in the way are 
a little <i>too</i> in the way.

411
00:26:45,340 --> 00:26:49,090
Why do you insist on aiming 
just below my chest every time?

412
00:26:49,090 --> 00:26:51,370
I suppose you could call it my hobby.

413
00:26:51,370 --> 00:26:53,090
I am the Bowel Hunter, after all.

414
00:26:53,090 --> 00:26:54,880
My hobby is cutting open bellies!

415
00:26:54,880 --> 00:26:56,890
The boss likes to say...

416
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:02,550
that the best defense is a good offense.

417
00:27:02,550 --> 00:27:07,270
So if I use a shield meant for 
defense to attack instead...

418
00:27:08,180 --> 00:27:11,890
The best defense and the 
best offense come together,

419
00:27:11,890 --> 00:27:15,570
making me the strongest one here, right?!

420
00:27:15,810 --> 00:27:18,820
Don't ya think so, Big Sis?

421
00:27:18,820 --> 00:27:20,480
Whoa, you're huge!

422
00:27:21,100 --> 00:27:23,080
Wait, are you my sister?!

423
00:27:23,080 --> 00:27:25,790
I feel like I should call 
you "Big Bro" instead.

424
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:29,950
Don't be so rude the moment 
we see each other again!

425
00:27:34,820 --> 00:27:37,550
Garf, you have grown quite big.

426
00:27:37,810 --> 00:27:40,530
That just sounds like sarcasm!

427
00:27:40,530 --> 00:27:43,430
You're the one who's way too damn huge!

428
00:27:43,890 --> 00:27:44,890
So...

429
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:48,980
Can I interrupt your happy reunion now?

430
00:27:48,980 --> 00:27:51,560
How nice of ya to wait for us.

431
00:27:51,860 --> 00:27:53,430
Yo, Sis—

432
00:27:53,430 --> 00:27:56,640
Big Sis, do you know a chick named Rem?

433
00:27:57,650 --> 00:27:59,620
Yes, she's in the mansion.

434
00:27:59,620 --> 00:28:01,780
Subaru-sama said she was Ram's sister.

435
00:28:02,210 --> 00:28:05,490
Get Rem outta here as soon 
as you get an opening.

436
00:28:05,490 --> 00:28:08,500
I'm gonna have my hands full with this bitch.

437
00:28:08,860 --> 00:28:09,830
What are you saying?

438
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:11,840
Sorry, Big Sis.

439
00:28:12,220 --> 00:28:16,420
She ain't the type I can take on 
while worryin' about who's behind me.

440
00:28:17,020 --> 00:28:17,970
Garf...

441
00:28:18,580 --> 00:28:21,050
You see my arm, don't ya?

442
00:28:21,450 --> 00:28:26,000
This is the shield you and I 
played with when we were kids.

443
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:31,790
It was runnin' with you that 
made me the strongest one there is.

444
00:28:38,900 --> 00:28:41,420
Bring it on, bitch in black!

445
00:28:41,420 --> 00:28:43,650
We'll celebrate me gettin' 
out of the Sanctuary!

446
00:28:43,990 --> 00:28:50,570
The first thing I'm gonna do is 
bash up the first wall in my way!

447
00:28:52,790 --> 00:28:55,790
Reunion of Roars

448
00:29:03,250 --> 00:29:07,020
Why are you here? I never called for you.

449
00:29:07,020 --> 00:29:11,270
Sorry, but I'm a guy who shows 
up whether he's been called or not.

450
00:29:11,530 --> 00:29:13,990
You are as self-serving as ever, I suppose.

451
00:29:13,990 --> 00:29:15,980
That's right. I'm selfish.

452
00:29:16,820 --> 00:29:19,120
I'm getting you out of here, Beatrice.

453
00:29:19,730 --> 00:29:24,240
This time, you're gonna let me 
drag you out into the sunlight,

454
00:29:24,520 --> 00:29:28,940
and then we're gonna play until your 
dress is black with mud!

455
00:29:28,940 --> 00:29:38,940


